{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start comes with its own ESLint plugin. This plugin is used to enforce best practices and help you avoid common mistakes when working with Server Components and server/client boundaries."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The plugin is a separate package that you need to install:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"bun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flat-config-eslint-config-js","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flat Config ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eslint.config.js"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The release of ESLint 9.0 introduced a new way to configure ESLint using a flat config format. The TanStack Start ESLint Plugin supports this format and provides a recommended config you can use to enable all recommended rules."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recommended-flat-config-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommended Flat Config setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To enable all recommended rules:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  pluginStart.configs['flat/recommended'],\n  // Any other config...\n]","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-flat-config-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Flat Config setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, load the plugin and configure only the rules you want:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  {\n    plugins: {\n      '@tanstack/start': pluginStart,\n    },\n    rules: {\n      '@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component': 'error',\n      '@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component': 'error',\n    },\n  },\n  // Any other config...\n]","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"legacy-config-eslintrc","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Legacy Config ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".eslintrc"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prior to ESLint 9.0, the most common way to configure ESLint was using a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".eslintrc"},{"type":"text","value":" file. The TanStack Start ESLint plugin still supports this configuration method."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recommended-legacy-config-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommended Legacy Config setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To enable all recommended rules, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extends"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"extends\": [\"plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended\"]\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-legacy-config-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Legacy Config setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" and configure the rules you want:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"plugins\": [\"@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\"],\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component\": \"error\",\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\"\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rules"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following rules are available in the TanStack Start ESLint plugin:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./no-client-code-in-server-component.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./no-async-client-component.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"flat-config-eslint-config-js","text":"Flat Config (eslint.config.js)","level":2},{"id":"recommended-flat-config-setup","text":"Recommended Flat Config setup","level":3},{"id":"custom-flat-config-setup","text":"Custom Flat Config setup","level":3},{"id":"legacy-config-eslintrc","text":"Legacy Config (.eslintrc)","level":2},{"id":"recommended-legacy-config-setup","text":"Recommended Legacy Config setup","level":3},{"id":"custom-legacy-config-setup","text":"Custom Legacy Config setup","level":3},{"id":"rules","text":"Rules","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Start comes with its own ESLint plugin. This plugin is used to enforce best practices and help you avoid common mistakes when working with Server Components and server/client boundaries.\n\n## Installation\n\nThe plugin is a separate package that you need to install:\n\n```sh\nnpm install -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\nbun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\n## Flat Config (`eslint.config.js`)\n\nThe release of ESLint 9.0 introduced a new way to configure ESLint using a flat config format. The TanStack Start ESLint Plugin supports this format and provides a recommended config you can use to enable all recommended rules.\n\n### Recommended Flat Config setup\n\nTo enable all recommended rules:\n\n```js\n// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  pluginStart.configs['flat/recommended'],\n  // Any other config...\n]\n```\n\n### Custom Flat Config setup\n\nAlternatively, load the plugin and configure only the rules you want:\n\n```js\n// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  {\n    plugins: {\n      '@tanstack/start': pluginStart,\n    },\n    rules: {\n      '@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component': 'error',\n      '@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component': 'error',\n    },\n  },\n  // Any other config...\n]\n```\n\n## Legacy Config (`.eslintrc`)\n\nPrior to ESLint 9.0, the most common way to configure ESLint was using a `.eslintrc` file. The TanStack Start ESLint plugin still supports this configuration method.\n\n### Recommended Legacy Config setup\n\nTo enable all recommended rules, add `plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended` in `extends`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"extends\": [\"plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Legacy Config setup\n\nAlternatively, add `@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start` to `plugins` and configure the rules you want:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plugins\": [\"@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\"],\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component\": \"error\",\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nThe following rules are available in the TanStack Start ESLint plugin:\n\n- [@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component](./no-client-code-in-server-component.md)\n- [@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component](./no-async-client-component.md)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: eslint-plugin-start\ntitle: ESLint Plugin Start\n---\n\nTanStack Start comes with its own ESLint plugin. This plugin is used to enforce best practices and help you avoid common mistakes when working with Server Components and server/client boundaries.\n\n## Installation\n\nThe plugin is a separate package that you need to install:\n\n```sh\nnpm install -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\nor\n\n```sh\nbun add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\n```\n\n## Flat Config (`eslint.config.js`)\n\nThe release of ESLint 9.0 introduced a new way to configure ESLint using a flat config format. The TanStack Start ESLint Plugin supports this format and provides a recommended config you can use to enable all recommended rules.\n\n### Recommended Flat Config setup\n\nTo enable all recommended rules:\n\n```js\n// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  pluginStart.configs['flat/recommended'],\n  // Any other config...\n]\n```\n\n### Custom Flat Config setup\n\nAlternatively, load the plugin and configure only the rules you want:\n\n```js\n// eslint.config.js\nimport pluginStart from '@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start'\n\nexport default [\n  {\n    plugins: {\n      '@tanstack/start': pluginStart,\n    },\n    rules: {\n      '@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component': 'error',\n      '@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component': 'error',\n    },\n  },\n  // Any other config...\n]\n```\n\n## Legacy Config (`.eslintrc`)\n\nPrior to ESLint 9.0, the most common way to configure ESLint was using a `.eslintrc` file. The TanStack Start ESLint plugin still supports this configuration method.\n\n### Recommended Legacy Config setup\n\nTo enable all recommended rules, add `plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended` in `extends`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"extends\": [\"plugin:@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start/recommended\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Legacy Config setup\n\nAlternatively, add `@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start` to `plugins` and configure the rules you want:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plugins\": [\"@tanstack/eslint-plugin-start\"],\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component\": \"error\",\n    \"@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component\": \"error\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nThe following rules are available in the TanStack Start ESLint plugin:\n\n- [@tanstack/start/no-client-code-in-server-component](./no-client-code-in-server-component.md)\n- [@tanstack/start/no-async-client-component](./no-async-client-component.md)\n"}
